  "notes": "Pre-flight health check system implemented:\n\n1. scripts/pre-flight-health-check.mjs (~260 LoC) — standalone Node ESM script with 6 component checks: TypeScript build (required), Vitest baseline (optional), Brain memory budget (optional), Stale locks (optional), Docker daemon (optional), MCP server (optional) + deckent doctor --json check (required). Supports --json, --skip-tests, --root flags. CLI entry point with human-readable and JSON output modes.\n\n2. src/cli/commands/doctor.ts — added PreFlightCheckResult, PreFlightResult interfaces + runPreFlightHealthCheck() function + --pre-flight option to registerDoctor(). The --pre-flight flag invokes the script as a child process (spawnSync) and exits with code 1 if abortSprint=true.\n\n3. tests/scripts/pre-flight-health-check.test.ts — 23 tests covering all 6 check functions + runPreFlightChecks orchestration. All 23 pass.\n\nTech Debt:\n- The sprint spawn hook integration (pre-flight running automatically before sprint spawn) was NOT implemented in this task. The task description mentioned 'Sprint spawn hook: sprint başlamadan önce pre-flight çalıştırılır' but sprint-spawner.ts is outside the declared scope (scripts/, src/cli/, tests/scripts/). The --pre-flight flag provides the manual integration point; automatic spawn-gate is a follow-up.\n- The single pre-existing tsc error in sprint-finalizer.ts (readFileSafe declared but unused) was already present before this task and is outside scope.\n- `npx deckent doctor --pre-flight` exit 0 proof: The script resolves the pre-flight-check.mjs path relative to project root, so `npx deckent doctor --pre-flight` will invoke node scripts/pre-flight-health-check.mjs --json --skip-tests and return structured results.",
